 foundling and in our new interview  he shared an  artist version of what his sister jill  might look like  assuming she too might have been  abandoned somewhere  and grew up not knowing her true  identity that  part of the quest is still alive and  open right the question of where  the quest for jill is it's on it's it's  ongoing and i'm not going to stop till  we find her  franzak has made considerable progress  on the other quest  too the search for the kidnapped baby  the i-team reported last december  that a man living in rural michigan had  been matched through dna  to the missing franzac a news team from  our affiliate wgn in chicago  followed the trail to the town of manton  michigan where they tracked down  and spoke to this man kevin beatty whose  family members suspected he might be the  missing franzac  when their dna tests leaked out various  investigators  including the fbi came to believe that  beatty  was biological paul beatty spoke to wgn  but asked them to keep his name private  because he was struggling with cancer  wgn agreed in nevada paul franzak  also honored that request and still  won't confirm to us  that beatty was franzac but he did  confirm  biological paul was alive as of a year  ago  and told us the franzac baby did reach  out to his long-suffering mother  dora franzak he actually talked to my  mom  they actually talked quite a few times  and unfortunately he passed away kevin  beatty died in april  the franzak family sent condolences  after his passing  george knapp 8 news now the other  unanswered question is who  kidnapped the franzac baby paul franzek  says he has some solid leads but is  still trying to crack that mystery  and we have additional links on our  website
 

